/**
 * PostHog product analytics through the first-party /ingest proxy (see posthog-proxy). Loads
 * on production only, like Google Tag Manager, so staging and local traffic stay out of the
 * project. Until the visitor accepts cookies, PostHog keeps its id in memory only (nothing is
 * stored); CookieBadge switches it to persistent storage on "Accept".
 * Events: pageviews, plan CTAs, app/contact/outbound clicks, theme toggles, chat opens, leads.
